course: dictionary
lesson: 12821
title: Emerging: coming out and coming up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word emerging comes from the verb emerge. To emerge means to come out from somewhere hidden or dark. «The sun slowly emerged from behind the clouds.» The sun was hidden, then it came out. The clues are slowly and from behind, which show it moved from hidden into view.
explain: Emerging can also describe something new that is starting to grow or become important. «The young artist is an emerging talent.» An emerging talent is not famous yet, but people are beginning to notice them. Ask yourself: is this thing new and growing? If yes, emerging probably means that.
explain: Sometimes emerging means that facts or ideas are becoming known. «New clues are emerging about the old ship.» Nobody knew these clues before, and now they are coming out into the open. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "new clues are becoming known" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Emerge means to come out from somewhere hidden or dark.
fact: «Emerging» is the -ing form of «emerge», so it can describe something that is coming out right now.
fact: As an adjective, «emerging» means new and beginning to grow or become important, like «an emerging country».
fact: In science, butterflies emerge from chrysalises and chicks emerge from eggs.
fact: «Emerging markets» are countries whose businesses are growing fast.
exercise: «The sun slowly emerged from behind the clouds.» What does emerged mean? | Sank under the sea | Stayed hidden forever | *Came out from somewhere hidden | Fell to the ground
exercise: Mia says «an emerging artist» is just a person who paints. What does emerging suggest? | *New and starting to become known | Very old and famous | Sleeping in a studio | Lost and forgotten
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the chick came out of the egg: «The chick emerged from its shell, wet and tired.» | shell | wet | *emerged | tired
test: «New facts are emerging about the dinosaurs.» What does emerging mean here? | Disappearing | Lost forever | *Becoming known | Cooking dinner
test: Dad's company invests in «emerging markets». What does emerging mean in that phrase? | Ancient and falling apart | *Growing and developing fast | Sleepy and quiet | Shut down
exam: Which sentence uses emerging as an adjective? | *The emerging technology will help doctors. | The sun went behind the hill. | The frog emerged from the pond at dawn. | The butterfly emerged from its chrysalis.
